    <j.2:abstract xml:lang="en-US">"The Physics of Black Holes" explores the fundamental principles governing black holes, including general relativity and quantum mechanics. This article examines their formation, properties, and the effects on surrounding space-time. By analyzing recent discoveries and theories, it aims to deepen our understanding of these enigmatic cosmic phenomena and their implications for astrophysics.</j.2:abstract>
